Given \( \vec{F}=5 \hat{i}+2 \hat{j}-5 \hat{k} ; \vec{r}=\hat{i}-2 \hat{j}+\hat{k} \)<br>We know torque<br>\[
\tau=\vec{r} \times \vec{F}=\left|\begin{array}{ccc}
\hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \\
1 & -2 & 1 \\
5 & 2 & -5
\end{array}\right|
\]<br>Therefore,<br>\[
\begin{array}{l}
\tau=\hat{i}(10-2)-\hat{j}(-5-5)+\hat{k}(2+10) \\
\Rightarrow \tau=8 \hat{i}+10 \hat{j}+12 \hat{k}
\end{array}
\]<br>Thus, torque about origin is \( 8 \hat{i}+10 \hat{j}+12 \hat{k} \)
